WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:02.660
More than a thousand years ago...

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:05.600
...there was a formal government organization in the city of Kyoto...

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.900
...called the Ministry of Onmyou Affairs.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.930
The technical employees who served there were called Onmyou mystics.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:17.510
From a modern perspective, the shady incantations, the spells...

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:19.350
...and the telling of fortunes...

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.650
...may be considered to be meaningless rituals based in superstition.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:26.760
However, back then, for those who had aspirations in science...

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.720
...it was the focal point of the newest technology...

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.720
...from both inside and outside Japan.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.890
It was also the one and only research institution that sought to thoroughly study...

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.600
...the basic sciences such as astronomy, geography, and meteorology.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.240
See? There's nothing.

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:28.150
Nothing. It's the pits.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.080
They said the construction people took it clean away.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:32.690
Ain't it just empty?

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:33.920
I can't take it.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.360
That was the crystallization of my six years in grade school.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:41.770
What's a guy who doesn't even play baseball doing just collecting the cards?

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:45.200
Things like the fruits of a geek's labor will be forever beyond me.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:48.300
It's not just the baseball cards.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:50.240
There are the vending machine toys...

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.310
...and the "Japan's Rare Animal Series"...

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:54.100
...that I went completely into debt to collect.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:56.010
All of it!

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:03.260
Gimme back my Iriomote cat!

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:07.050
Sasshi, you just moved into a brand new condo last month.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:09.620
Didn't you take it all with you over there?

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.360
At the new place, I've been prohibited from bringing any of my geeky fruits of labor.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:18.240
Cuz it's mega small.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:23.030
And I hadn't heard anything about the house being torn down while I was away at camp.

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.770
It's the pits.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:29.290
All I can do now is go home, eat a yam, fart and go to sleep.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.290
I can understand that it's a shock...

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.880
...but no matter what, being human, having your health is what's most important.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.000
Well, see ya later.

00:02:58.210 --> 00:02:59.030
Ya know...

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:04.270
...there's one other mega shocking thing that got decided while you were away at camp.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:08.620
I see. So, it's finally been decided. Finally?

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.090
You're talking about this condo getting torn down, too, right?

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.720
Yup, yup, and it was only just built too!

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:14.980
Hey, what the heck?!

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.060
Our shop, Grill Pelican, is moving out too.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:23.030
But the Pelican is still gonna stay put for a long time to come!

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:24.050
Masa-jii said so!

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:26.400
That's what Masa-jii's been saying, but...

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.370
Uh-huh.

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:31.070
Dad's been offered a job at a hotel restaurant.

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:32.130
Uh-huh.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:35.470
You know how dad trained to cook in France.

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:38.410
He's saying he wants to work some place with proper facilities.

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:40.140
Uh-huh.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:42.710
It's been decided.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.420
Uh-huh.

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:54.390
Well, congratulations for that.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.330
So, you're gonna be moving away.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:00.690
Yeah.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:15.340
Say, what about school? You transferring?

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:18.410
Weren't you gonna go home, fart and go to sleep?

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:22.220
How the heck am I supposed to fart after hearing what you told me?

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:25.130
Things that come out and things that swell happen when they happen.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:26.320
Well, don't worry.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:29.400
I'll be attending the school here for a bit of the second semester.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.130
So, where're you moving to?

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:35.670
Lake Akan.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:36.910
Lake Akan?

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:40.100
Lake Akan Tourist Hotel in Hokkaido.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.040
Hokkaido?

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.840
The Hokkaido where the salmon spawn and return?

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:47.140
We're supposed to go there by boat.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:48.850
It's mega far.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:52.810
But they've got Hokkaido foxes and marimo moss.

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:54.560
You can live anywhere.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:58.290
Being human, having your health is what's most important.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:10.570
I'm home!

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.040
Bon jour.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.010
Welcome back.

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:17.270
Sasshi, set the lit sign outside for me.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.250
I just got here and you're using me already?

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.150
Quit grumbling.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:24.980
Kids should just shut up and help the adults with their business.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:28.550
But I ain't your kid, Masa-jii.

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:29.960
Fool!

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:33.060
Anyone born around these parts, from the oldest one here...

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:36.660
...to Hiro-pon's grandkid Fumiya, are all kids of the shopping arcade!

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:40.470
You all grew up carrying the portable shrine at the Seimei Shrine every year!

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:41.610
Is that so?

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:44.610
Say Masa-jii...

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:47.610
...what are ya gonna do about carrying the portable shrine at the festival this year?

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:49.700
Doing, nothing.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.540
I'll be doing what I do every year.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:57.410
But you're gonna close down this shop and move overseas with everyone, right?

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:00.520
Everyone? What everyone?!

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:04.330
Don't you worry, I won't be shutting down the Pelican.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.460
Non, non, non.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.860
You're still saying that, Papa?!

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.990
Being stubborn like that isn't tres bien.

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:14.230
With all due respect, what in hell do you think one old man can do alone?!

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:17.670
That tres bien talk again?!

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:20.020
Papa, this le marché...

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:22.800
It's very, very sad that this market will disappear...

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:26.410
...but arguing against something that's been decided is Dadaism!

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:30.490
They're gonna tear down all the other houses...

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:33.080
...we can't be the only ones to stay standing about!

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:37.760
I need you to wise up already, you stubborn old man!

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:41.500
Like hell I'm gonna stand for your lectures with bad French mixed in!

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.800
All this time I ran this shop with your dead ma.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:46.630
I ain't gonna let it close down while I'm still kicking!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.800
And what the hell is with this redevelopment?!

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:53.100
These parts were finished developing fifty years ago!

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:57.300
Moron! What's finished is your brain, you dimwit!

00:06:57.510 --> 00:06:59.270
What?! Dimwit?!

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:01.180
What's French about that?!

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:03.750
Let's hear ya say that again, you little...

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:13.890
I heard your grandma used to be just like Masa-jii.

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:18.460
Yeah, she was sitting at the front desk right up until the night before she went in her coffin.

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:20.270
Did ya know?

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:24.100
About how my grandpa had a crush on your grandma?

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:25.940
No way!

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:28.100
Well, it's back when they were kids, though.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:32.610
Oh, you scared me there, 'cause I thought it was something recent.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:36.110
It'd be just bad if she came back to haunt us over that.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:39.190
But hadn't you ever heard anything from your grandma?

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:40.490
From my grandma?

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:42.990
This is just a woman's intuition, ya know?

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:46.480
But I think Masa-jii and your grandma are hiding something.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:50.520
She didn't seem like she had anything to hide.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:54.970
Oh, come to think of it, grandpa was always complaing about how...

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:58.670
...grandma had the hots for someone else before they got married.

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:02.290
Way I hear, some egghead who made this shopping arcade.

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:05.500
Made this place? You mean, like the person who designed it?

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:08.000
Maybe it was someone from a municipal office.

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:12.790
Back when she was in school, grandma made lunch everyday and visited him.

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:14.510
I wonder what kind of guy this egghead was?

00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:17.620
An egghead who made this shopping arcade?

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.020
Never even heard of him.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:24.130
Yeah? There's no way Masa-jii wouldn't know the guy...

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:27.650
...which means, they were serious romantic rivals and he's still bitter about it!

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:30.650
I guess my grandma was real popular.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:43.750
Way I hear, she had big, honking boobs and a nice figure!

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:47.280
And creamy skin to boot!

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:48.410
Pervert.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:52.250
You idiot!

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:53.260
Mercy!

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:03.260
You can't see this pelican sign from the street at all!

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:05.170
What's the point?

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:08.270
Man, my hat fell down there.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:11.600
What the hell are you doing changing the subject?!

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:15.950
I'm done!

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:18.550
Sayaka, you're finished already?

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:20.020
I'm dieting right now.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:21.790
Dieting?

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:25.230
Man, if they're gonna redevelop this place anyway...

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:27.400
...I wish they'd make it cool like Shibuya.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:30.100
Moron! People couldn't live in a place like that!

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.570
I want a big supermarket.

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:34.290
There's the department store!

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:37.070
It costs way too much to shop at the department store.

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:40.010
I couldn't get by without the clearance sales at supermarkets.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:43.740
Satoshi, did that Masa-bou say anything?

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.870
Masa-jii?

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.350
Well, he's the same as grandma.

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:53.720
He's saying he won't take down the store sign as long as he's kicking...

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:55.350
...even if they're the last store standing.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:59.620
He's as kooky as ever. There's no point in holding out on your own.

00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:01.100
Point?

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:04.220
Speaking of which, there's a turtle on top of the bathhouse, too.

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:06.270
There's a bird over at Arumi's.

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:07.970
Do those have any point to them?

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:11.460
There's no point to those signs if the customers can't see them.

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:14.540
Point, eh?

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:17.280
The Turtle Bath and Masa-bou's Pelican...

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:19.970
...are the linchpins of Abenobashi Shopping Arcade.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:23.280
But with everyone cleared out of there now...

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:27.250
...I suppose it's just more odd talking about the point and the like.

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:33.360
How long're you gonna take to eat?

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.830
It definitely feels like there's something to it.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.260
Why don't you just ask him straight up?

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:46.210
Oh...

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:50.080
Well, you know, I'm not sure if a kid should be asking about it.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:51.880
There's just that feel to it.

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:56.260
Grandpa's being obstinate about staying behind by himself.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:57.970
Masa-jii's staying behind?

00:10:58.450 --> 00:10:59.920
Of course, we can't do that.

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:02.020
It's a mega headache for the whole family.

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:05.790
Dad's actually real sad about leaving too, after all.

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:08.320
That was good!

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:09.140
Thanks a bunch.

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:11.830
Aren't you sad?

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:13.100
Not a bit.

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:14.540
"Where you live is home."

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.970
Being human, having your health is what's most important.

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:20.300
Oh, but there is something that's gonna be rough.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:22.640
I don't like the cold.

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:28.050
But I also sorta feel it's not good to uproot grandpa against his will...

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:26.880
Really? That must be disappointing.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:28.050
It's no big deal, really.

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:30.890
...and drag him off to some other place.

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:30.890
Thanks a bunch!

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:34.150
Hey, Arumi-chan!

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:36.550
Beautiful as ever, aren't ya?

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:39.010
Hello, Mister.

00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:44.560
So, you're gonna let Masa-jii stay here 'cause of his old crush?

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:48.640
No, that's important, too...

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:52.570
...but I feel like something even more messed up would happen if Masa-jii left.

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:54.540
Something even more messed up?

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:57.520
Like Abenobashi being overrun by kogals in mini-skirts?

00:11:58.280 --> 00:11:58.860
What's that?

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:00.610
Aniki's wish.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:03.380
Ain't that more like your wish?

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:04.890
No, it ain't.

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:06.120
Hey there, you two.

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:11.370
You two always get along so well.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:13.660
Afternoon, Aki-neechan.

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:15.210
Dearie, it's still good morning for me.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:18.270
When Arumi-chan leaves this place...

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:22.100
...it's gonna feel like another light's gone out 'round here.

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:25.400
I'll bet you'll be lonely when she leaves.

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:27.970
No way, not at all!

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:31.010
There you go, letting your foolish pride get in the way.

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:35.810
Even when they're this small, men are just so cute!

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:38.980
Say, Aki-nee...

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:42.310
...you've been friends with Sasshi's family for a long time, right?

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:43.740
Yes, I have.

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:48.950
The lady at the Turtle Bath has been kind to me since I was young.

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:53.090
Who ever thought she'd pass away so soon?

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:55.710
Um, there's something I'd like to ask you.

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:57.570
What is it?

00:12:57.840 --> 00:13:01.830
Was there some shady relationship between my grandpa and Sasshi's grandma?

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:04.710
You're still drinking that thing?

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:07.050
No, that's not it.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:11.050
See, see, what Arumi's trying to say isn't about past triangle relationships or lunches.

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:13.150
It's not about that, but you see, well...

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:14.750
Let's see...

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:17.450
There, there. Calm down and drink some ramune.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:19.280
Okay.

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:24.820
Do you know how our two houses are related? Like their positions?

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:28.960
And about a turtle and a bird being the linchpins of the shopping arcade.

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:30.580
A turtle and a bird?

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:31.660
Right.

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:33.160
I know.

00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:34.540
What?!

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.880
It's posted at Seimei's.

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.250
It's called the harmony of the four gods.

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:47.480
A turtle, a bird, a dragon, and a tiger.

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:50.990
This is it.

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:55.000
A turtle...

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:57.190
...and a bird.

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:11.180
Harmony of the four gods.

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:13.880
So, basically, it's lucky for places...

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:15.370
...to have these things in the four cardinal directions.

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:18.830
Looks like it could fit Abeno Ginza just right.

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:20.770
In the north is Genbu...

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:23.090
The turtle is the Turtle Bath that your family runs.

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:25.030
In the south is Suzaku...

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.750
When it comes to a bird in the south...

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:28.350
That'd be our pelican.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:30.320
Then, what about the western edge?

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:33.350
Oh!

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:36.130
Tiger's Gold Coin Dumplings!

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:37.770
Which means...

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:39.100
Lessee, lessee, lessee...

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:41.190
It's like this, right? And like this, so...

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:43.040
The Seiryu in the east...

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:44.530
Ryu, dragon...

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:46.280
Dragon's Wooden Clog Shop!

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:47.280
I see!

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:49.150
That means...

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:52.180
We're the only one left.

00:14:52.650 --> 00:14:56.450
The thing I don't get is how this is related to Masa-jii's kooky attitude.

00:14:58.430 --> 00:14:59.890
How it's related...

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.260
All right! Let's go ask him directly!

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:04.770
Yeah! It's the only thing to do!

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:05.960
You're right!

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:13.890
I knew it!

00:15:14.710 --> 00:15:16.940
That bastard's sleeping there again!

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:20.250
Hey, get down!

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:23.240
Ya can't sleep there!

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:25.820
Get down!

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:27.860
You bastard!

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:29.760
You listening to me?!

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:32.020
Why you! Take that and that!

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:32.820
You little!

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:42.750
Damn fat cat!

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:47.110
This here is the precious bird spirit!

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:49.400
You thickheaded bastard!

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.730
Arumi, you're too fast!

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:12.700
You're just too slow!

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:15.070
What the heck is this?!

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:20.360
Arumi! Sasshi!

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:23.180
Masa-jii!

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:30.180
Don't fall!

00:16:51.640 --> 00:16:53.110
What?

00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:54.940
A thief?

00:16:58.310 --> 00:16:59.620
The Pelican...

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:04.020
Papa!

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:06.410
Arumi!

00:17:06.490 --> 00:17:08.190
Arumi! What happened to Masa-jii?!

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:10.280
Sasshi, call an ambulance! Telephone! Telephone!

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:19.100
He fell hard on his hip, so he should get some quiet rest for a while.

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:22.000
Thank you for everything.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.520
Please take care.

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:29.520
Watch for a chance and make sure you set him straight, all right?

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:31.510
I know!

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:33.300
But this is enough for today!

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:45.690
Oh, it's a bird.

00:19:06.970 --> 00:19:07.870
So?

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:12.170
What'd you do after you saw the so-called dragon?

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:14.840
I fell asleep again.

00:19:15.650 --> 00:19:17.880
Give the tall tales a rest.

00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:21.140
If it were true, how the heck could you go to sleep after seeing a dragon?

00:19:21.790 --> 00:19:24.720
Yeah, but no one else was up yet...

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:26.490
...and I was sleepy.

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:29.860
Of course, you were. 'Cause you were dreaming.

00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:33.460
It wasn't a dream! It was totally real!

00:19:34.670 --> 00:19:38.100
The messed up stuff you were talking about is happening right now!

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:40.970
'Cause our pelican broke?

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:43.630
What did Masa-jii say?

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:46.380
Nothing.

00:19:46.380 --> 00:19:48.410
Did you ask him about the harmony of the four gods?

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:50.650
I can't ask about that.

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:53.520
And it doesn't matter anymore.

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:58.720
What do you mean that it doesn't matter?

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:01.420
Grandpa's getting out of the hospital next week.

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:05.700
Oh, I see. So, that's it.

00:20:06.400 --> 00:20:09.340
He's already given up on keeping the restaurant up...

00:20:09.340 --> 00:20:11.740
...and it's been decided that we're all going to Hokkaido, so...

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:14.520
So, you're all going.

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:17.340
I'm glad.

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:20.440
I'm sorry, Sasshi.

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:22.030
Why're you apologizing?

00:20:23.350 --> 00:20:25.050
It doesn't make any sense.

00:20:26.390 --> 00:20:28.120
But even after you transfer to Lake Akan...

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:31.730
Mu...

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:32.750
Mu?

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:36.230
Mu!

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:38.670
Mu...

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:40.260
Mushrooms?

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:41.550
Mushrooms...

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.270
What the hell was that?!

00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:46.840
That was, that was...

00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:47.910
What was it?!

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:48.510
Starting from the left...

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:49.260
...shitake...

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:49.850
...matsutake...

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:50.640
...death cap...

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:51.600
...pig's ears...

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:52.600
...usukimorinokasa...

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:53.850
...urabenihotei shimeji...

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:54.980
...kichahouraitake!

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:58.090
How educational! G'bye!

00:20:58.090 --> 00:21:00.450
Wait for me!

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:03.650
Arumi, don't leave me behind!

00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:10.760
Doesn't the town seem awfully flat somehow?!

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:13.160
It's just your imagination!

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:27.370
What kinda joke is this?

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:31.150
What?! What?!

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:03.370
Where the heck are we?

00:22:05.890 --> 00:22:07.620
Talk about an impressive castle.

00:22:08.390 --> 00:22:10.220
Is it a love hotel?

00:22:10.220 --> 00:22:11.600
This is the pits.

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:46.450
Preview time!

00:23:46.450 --> 00:23:48.120
Arumi, it's the preview! The preview for the next episode!

00:23:48.120 --> 00:23:49.520
What're ya so excited about?

00:23:49.520 --> 00:23:51.910
It's been my dream to do a next episode preview.

00:23:51.910 --> 00:23:52.830
You're weird.

00:23:52.830 --> 00:23:54.730
Lemme do the preview. Do ya mind? Do ya mind? Huh? Huh?

00:23:54.730 --> 00:23:55.800
Just do it.

00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:57.430
Okay, okay, okay, here goes, here goes.

00:23:57.430 --> 00:24:00.590
I don't really care, but can't you do something about looking like a dope?

00:24:00.730 --> 00:24:03.540
Your pants're uneven, you've got stains from spilled food on your shirt...

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:05.940
...you've got a booger hanging from your nose, and your face is moronic.

00:24:05.940 --> 00:24:08.480
We've only just started. You gotta shape up a little, ya know?

00:24:08.010 --> 00:24:09.110
Wait, wait...

00:24:08.480 --> 00:24:11.180
And say, you're gonna run out of time if you don't hurry up and do the preview.

00:24:13.480 --> 00:24:14.640
Next time!
